This project is extracted from, and generalises, RLCD (Reinforcement Learning Calibrated Decision), the
decision service of the View Engine project by the same author (MIT License). Reused from that reference
implementation: the System One-compatible wire contract and its confidence formulas, the calibration
metrics and skill test design, the Beta-Bernoulli posterior ledger and binomial / Wilson evidence gates,
time-ordered purged calibration folds, and the feedback loop design. No trading logic is included.

The wire contract follows the public documentation of Typesafe's "System One" evaluation API (one
evaluation endpoint, three question types, the same confidence formulas). Open RLCD is not affiliated
with Typesafe.

Default text encoder (downloaded on first use, not redistributed in this repository):
- intfloat/multilingual-e5-small (https://huggingface.co/intfloat/multilingual-e5-small), MIT License.
  Wang et al., "Multilingual E5 Text Embeddings: A Technical Report", 2024.
